7) what the frontier says, in the units the claims around it are made in

   tfidf:
   - top_k is inert while the budget keeps one passage: 1 -> 8 moves the ceiling by at most 0.000 of rho and the prompt by 0.1 words, because 1.03-1.03 passages survive whichever way the candidates were ranked
   - the finer chunking buys ceiling per prompt word most cheaply: 45/10 keeps 2.27 passages in 196.1 prompt words and reaches ceiling rho +0.916 against the shipped rho +0.732 at 173.4 words, i.e. +0.184 of ceiling for +22.7 prompt words (+13.1%)
   - reaching ceiling 0.90 by widening the budget instead costs 246.8 words
   - cheapest cell at ceiling rho >= 0.90 per axis: budget 180 at 247 words, chunk 45/10 at 196 words; top_k never reaches it at any value swept here
   - across all 6 chunkings the floor costs at most 10.1 points of delivered proof (one chunk per CV, where one coarse chunk can fail every requirement at once and 5 of 30 CVs are left with no passage at all) and 0.5 at the shipped one, while it raises the requirements marked `none` by 2.63 to 3.97 per CV - so at every geometry it buys claim discipline rather than evidence

   dense:
   - top_k is inert while the budget keeps one passage: 1 -> 8 moves the ceiling by at most 0.000 of rho and the prompt by 0.4 words, because 1.13-1.13 passages survive whichever way the candidates were ranked
   - the finer chunking buys ceiling per prompt word most cheaply: 45/10 keeps 2.43 passages in 205.5 prompt words and reaches ceiling rho +0.889 against the shipped rho +0.804 at 181.0 words, i.e. +0.084 of ceiling for +24.6 prompt words (+13.6%)
   - reaching ceiling 0.90 by widening the budget instead costs 257.7 words
   - cheapest cell at ceiling rho >= 0.90 per axis: budget 180 at 258 words, chunk 150/30 at 209 words; top_k never reaches it at any value swept here
   - across all 6 chunkings the floor costs no delivered proof at all (largest loss 0.0 points), and raises the requirements marked `none` by 1.40 to 2.77 per CV - claim discipline only, at every geometry

